  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively establish the relevant FCC/B2 lamellar eutectic alloy, show that processing can transform HEA phase architectures, and identify coherent or hierarchical interfaces and multiple deformation modes as routes to combined strength and ductility. Particularly relevant are coherent interfaces in nearly the same Al-Co-Cr-Fe-Ni system (R17), coherent BCC/B2 relationships (R11), and hierarchical coherent precipitations with improved strength and ductility (R19). R20 also combines pressure-assisted consolidation with high temperature. However, none describes HPHT treatment in a hexahedron-anvil apparatus for the Al0.7CoCrFeNi eutectic alloy, nor the specific conversion to a coherent hierarchical FCC/B2 pattern with preferential FCC-to-B2 dislocation transfer. Selecting HPHT as the route therefore requires a substantial new idea, although the records point toward its intended microstructural and mechanical rationale."
